title: The Circles Petition
subtitle: The magi circles bring their case to the government...
view-if: year >= 1930 and marcher_in_government and magi_petition_seen == 0 and (magi_registry_repealed or magi_circles_recognized or bvp_relation >= 20)
on-arrival: magi_petition_seen = 1
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
tags: event

= The Circles Petition

A delegation of the magi circles has come to the capital — robed, careful, and very well briefed. Their petition is modest on its face: standing before the ordinary courts, relief from the registry's lingering indignities, and an end to the quiet bar that keeps their kind from the civil service's upper floors. Behind it stands the older question the republic has never answered: whether the magi are citizens who happen to work wonders, or a problem to be managed.

[? if bvp_relation >= 30: The <span style="color: #A2D8E0;">**Arcanists**</span> have let it be known, discreetly, that they would receive any courtesy shown the delegation as a courtesy shown to them. ?]The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> are already drafting their response to whatever we do.

- @grant: Receive the delegation and take up their petition.
- @quiet: Promise study — and deliver delay.
- @refuse: Turn them away. The coalition cannot bear this fight now.

@grant
on-arrival: magi_balance += 6 if magi_balance < 100; bvp_relation += 4*(1-dissent); faithful_marcher -= 2; unionist_relation -= 3; royalist_relation -= 2

The delegation is received in the chancellery's long gallery, photographed on the steps, and sent home with a commitment of substance. The circles' journals print the pictures for a month. The Faithful's pulpits and the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> press print them rather longer.

@quiet
on-arrival: magi_balance += 1 if magi_balance < 100; bvp_relation -= 2

A commission is struck, a chairman named, a report promised for a season that never quite arrives. The circles have seen this instrument before and know precisely what it is. Nothing is lost, little is gained, and the question keeps.

@refuse
on-arrival: magi_balance -= 6; bvp_relation -= 6; unionist_relation += 2; faithful_marcher += 2

The delegation is not received. The coalition's right breathes out; the circles go home to tell their halls what the republic's friendship is worth. Some of their younger members draw conclusions we may meet again, in harder company.
